(Raj:)Just that
I'm definitely not gay.

3
00:00:14,670 --> 00:00:16,940
(Sheldon:)SHELDON
Penny!

4
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:19,700
Penny! Penny!

5
00:00:19,710 --> 00:00:20,610
(Penny:)What's wrong?

6
00:00:20,610 --> 00:00:23,110
(Sheldon:)Nothing.
I was acting.

7
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:25,980
(Penny:)You were acting.

8
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:28,460
(Sheldon:)Yes. In preparation
for today's studies,

9
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:30,680
I read Stanislavski's
An Actor Prepares,

10
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:32,850
Stella Adler's
The Technique of Acting,

11
00:00:32,850 --> 00:00:34,420
Uta Hagen's
Respect for Acting,

12
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:37,790
and Henry Winkler's
Ayyy, I'm an Actor.

13
00:00:37,790 --> 00:00:39,690
(Penny:)Well, good for you.

14
00:00:39,690 --> 00:00:41,640
(Penny:)Come on in.

15
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:42,760
(Sheldon:)How shall we begin?

16
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:44,460
(Penny:)Well, I thought we'd start

17
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:46,930
(Sheldon:)with some
basic movement exercises.

18
00:00:46,930 --> 00:00:48,770
(Penny:)You know, get our bodies
warmed up a little.

19
00:00:48,770 --> 00:00:50,000
(Sheldon:)All right.

20
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:51,170
(Penny:)So I just want you to relax

21
00:00:51,170 --> 00:00:53,040
(Penny:)and kind of
move around in the space.

22
00:00:53,040 --> 00:01:03,020
(Penny:)You know,
just do whatever feels natural.

